=== P3 Feature view 0076 HighlightCard (Android) ===
--- NOTES (honesty covenant) ---
Capability: Kotlin 2.4.0 / AGP 8.9.2 / Compose BOM 2026.04.01 / Material 3 (libs.versions.toml).
  Satisfies the prompt's 'Jetpack Compose + Material 3, Kotlin 2.2.x' floor (newer line).
Module path: this Gradle build names the app module ':android' (settings.gradle.kts L33-34 states
  every P3/A* gate addresses ':android:'); the prompt template's ':app:' is that alias. Gate run below
  uses ':android:' verbatim, exactly as every predecessor 0001-0067 log does.
Web source: features/analytics/components/weekly-digest/HighlightCard.tsx is purely presentational
  (props only, no data hook, no t() calls). Per the AchievementBadge/ToolCard/SummaryStatsRow precedent,
  loading/error/stale/offline lifecycle lives on the owning page; modelling it here would be drift. The
  branches the source defines (optional change present/absent x positive/negative, optional subtitle) are
  the complete rendered state set and are each reproduced + tested.
Parity nuance (color/glow): the web maps color -> glowMap -> GlassPanel glow, but glowClasses are gated
  behind GlassPanel's 'hover' prop (hover && glowClasses[glow]) and HighlightCard never passes hover, so
  the accent has NO resting visual effect in the source. The neutral panel is rendered for every accent;
  glowMap is still modelled + unit-tested (HighlightCardProjection.glowFor) so the one source derivation
  is faithfully ported (reproduce-the-quirk discipline, not silent drift). The 5-key color->design-token
  mapping is shared with ToolCard (cyan->status.info, green->status.success, purple->chart.power,
  amber->status.warning, red->status.danger).
i18n (P1/S10): the surface is anonymous with ZERO catalog keys of its own - every visible string
  (label/value/change.value/subtitle) is a caller-provided, already-localized prop, matching the web
  source which has no t() calls. Acceptance 'every source i18n key has a catalog key' is vacuously met.
androidTest disclosure: the per-state UI + a11y test (HighlightCardUiTest.kt) is authored and compiles
  CLEAN for this surface (compileDebugAndroidTestKotlin reports zero errors attributable to it). The
  androidTest source set as a whole does NOT currently compile due to a PRE-EXISTING, repo-wide breakage
  in ~70 sibling files that import unresolved 'assertDoesNotExist'/'assertExists' - symbols this surface
  does not use. Those files are outside this artifact's allowed files, and the gate below compiles/runs
  UNIT tests only (never androidTest), so this condition is non-gating and is disclosed rather than hidden.
--- END NOTES ---

